# Licence

This repository contains two different things under two different licences.

## The data: CC BY 4.0

Everything in `data/`, and everything published at https://crawlindex.org derived from it,
is licensed under the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International licence.

https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/

You may copy, redistribute, transform and build upon it, including commercially. The only
condition is attribution:

> CrawlIndex by Fidget Labs BV. https://crawlindex.org. Licensed CC BY 4.0.

Please also include the measurement date alongside any figure you quote, so the claim
stays checkable as the index moves.

## The code: all rights reserved

Copyright (c) 2026 Fidget Labs BV. All rights reserved.

Everything that is not in `data/` is source code, and no licence is granted for it. It is
published so that the methodology behind the data is auditable: you can read it, check
that the numbers are produced the way the methodology page claims, and recompute any score
from a stored observation to verify it.

You may not copy, modify, redistribute or create derivative works of the code without
prior written permission from Fidget Labs BV.

Being able to verify how a public dataset is produced does not require the right to take
the software. The data is the gift; the code is the receipt.

### On forking

GitHub's Terms of Service grant every user the ability to view and fork any public
repository, and that permission cannot be revoked by a repository owner. Forking this
repository is therefore technically possible and not a violation of GitHub's terms.

It grants you no licence to the code. The fork button copies bytes; it does not transfer
rights. Running, modifying, publishing or building a product on this code still requires
written permission, and none is given here.

The data in `data/` is the exception, and it is genuinely yours to take: CC BY 4.0, no
permission needed, attribution only.

## Contact

There is no support address for this project by design. To remove a domain from the index,
disallow `CrawlIndexBot` in its robots.txt; the crawler checks that before requesting
anything else and the domain drops out on the next run.
